WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.670
Deleting hand-written

00:00:01.482 --> 00:00:02.944
GPU assembly made

00:00:02.756 --> 00:00:03.828
kernels better

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.166
glm-vx runs GLM

00:00:05.977 --> 00:00:07.227
models with GPU

00:00:07.039 --> 00:00:08.170
kernels written in

00:00:07.982 --> 00:00:08.630
Vx

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:09.998
which held 99

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.071
pieces of hand-written

00:00:10.883 --> 00:00:12.640
PTX across 25

00:00:12.451 --> 00:00:13.123
files

00:00:13.654 --> 00:00:14.585
They moved most

00:00:14.397 --> 00:00:15.529
to MLIR ops

00:00:15.668 --> 00:00:16.846
Fourteen of 20

00:00:16.658 --> 00:00:17.813
pinned kernels kept

00:00:17.696 --> 00:00:18.733
every instruction

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:19.783
and six got

00:00:19.595 --> 00:00:20.608
fewer because the

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.835
compiler could finally

00:00:21.646 --> 00:00:22.401
see around the

00:00:22.212 --> 00:00:22.754
code

00:00:23.294 --> 00:00:24.402
No kernel needs

00:00:24.214 --> 00:00:25.605
more registers one

00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:26.442
spill dropped from

00:00:26.254 --> 00:00:27.209
40 bytes to

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:27.539
8

00:00:27.657 --> 00:00:28.706
and all hardware

00:00:28.518 --> 00:00:29.650
tests passed on

00:00:29.461 --> 00:00:30.794
an H200

00:00:31.326 --> 00:00:32.340
Full story on

00:00:32.151 --> 00:00:33.047
the dashboard
